// Kai's First Strike Ascension (Passive line 3/3) - see docs/kai-ascensions.md. Bonus damage on a
// target's first-ever hit from an owner holding this upgrade, read live in
// DamageUtility.ResolveOutgoingDamage - gated on the OWNER holding this trait (not "has anyone ever
// hit this enemy"), so another hero's shot landing first in co-op doesn't silently deny Kai his own
// bonus.
//
// Each enemy triggers First Strike exactly ONCE, ever. An earlier design let the mark expire after a
// few untouched seconds, which turned an assassination mechanic into a damage-over-time rotation
// against the same target; rank 3's payoff is instead about CHAINING targets - see
// KillEmpowerBonus below.
component FirstStrikeUpgrade
{
    FP DamageMultiplierBonus;

    // Rank 3 only (0 at ranks 1-2). Killing an enemy that still carries this owner's own FirstStrike
    // mark empowers the NEXT First Strike by this much on top of DamageMultiplierBonus - the reward
    // for actually finishing the target you opened on, and what makes switching targets the strong
    // play rather than tunnelling one. See KaiFirstStrikeSystem.
    FP KillEmpowerBonus;

    // Live one-shot state, not authored: set to KillEmpowerBonus on a First-Strike kill, consumed
    // (back to 0) by the next First Strike hit. Deliberately non-stacking - a second kill before
    // spending it re-arms the same bonus rather than doubling it, so a chain of kills can't compound
    // into an unbounded multiplier.
    FP PendingEmpowerBonus;
}

// Lives on the TARGET, replacing the old bare KaiFirstStruck tag - same RevengeMark-shaped pattern
// (see Heroes/Max/Vendetta.qtn) so this can genuinely track WHICH Kai most recently claimed the mark,
// not just "has this enemy ever been hit." A second Kai's hit reclaims the mark (MarkedBy overwritten)
// rather than tracking both simultaneously - matches RevengeMark's own precedent. Never expires and
// is never removed while the enemy lives; the enemy dying is what clears it.
component FirstStrikeMark
{
    EntityRef MarkedBy;
}
